{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791590640,"nonce":"XLHJh4GRrGrj9+QSz59rFwNxA9k=","title":"Base UI adapter on the JSX runtime, and the interactive wiki built on it","message":"Purpose: a worked example for framework developers of an adapter on the host interface, and the base of blinc_ts's interactive wiki. Developers run it locally and learn the API from working examples, not from a web doc. It does not cover all of Base UI, only the components the wiki needs. Examples may add custom styles that are not Base UI's.\n\nDecisions\n- Lives in adapters/base-ui/, beside the JSX and Vue adapters. Palettes are not core (6e33649, comment 4), so the theme belongs to the adapter and not to src/theme.\n- Base UI parts draw nothing themselves. Components expose state as data-* attributes and sheets style them through the theme's variables.\n\nConstraints found while reading the engine (blinc_abi, as pinned here)\n- The host gives the cascade these states: hover, active, focus, focus-visible, focus-within, disabled, enabled. The engine also parses checked, indeterminate, required and others, but nothing sets them. A component must mirror its state into an attribute ([data-checked]) and not rely on :checked.\n- Attribute selectors, :is, :where, :has, nesting, @media, @import, @mixin, @include and @keyframes parse. Any other at-rule is skipped with a warning (no @layer, @supports, @font-face, @property).\n- The host draws background, color, opacity, border-radius, border-color, visibility, corner-shape and box-shadow, plus text properties. var() works inside box-shadow. host.ts does not read transition; motion is tracked in 35f7bd0.\n- A :root rule paints the whole window and its colour and font inherit, so a bundle's css can carry a base rule.\n- Font stacks resolve as a browser's do: the first installed family, else the first generic keyword. A theme can name a preferred face with safe fallbacks.\n\nDone: the theme\n- adapters/base-ui/theme.ts exports baseUiTheme, a light and dark ThemeBundle: warm paper and charcoal neutrals, teal primary, ember accent, the squircle reference shape (0.4, 3.3, 12), and a base :root sheet.\n- adapters/test/base-ui-theme.mjs checks every token in both schemes, WCAG contrast of 31 pairings per scheme (text 4.5, strong text 7, UI parts 3), a clean sheet load, and a rendered specimen by pixel, with a scheme switch leaving geometry unchanged. Specimen PNGs land in .blinc/base-ui-theme/.\n- Mutating the compiled theme (a mislabelled scheme, no root background, a misspelt variable, unreadable surfaces) fails the test each time.\n\nNext\n- Decide the component set from the wiki's outline.\n- JSX components for those parts, with their state machines in TypeScript (5c5fdd5).\n- A component stylesheet in the bundle's css, reading the theme variables.\n- The wiki shell: navigation, live example panes, source view.","files":null}]}